fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 . We give the name }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 genus }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 to the groups of races, called species, brought together following a consideration of their interconnections and constituting thus small limited series by the characteristics with which one chooses arbitrarily to define them.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 When a }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 genus }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 is created well, all the races or species which it includes are similar in their most essential and most numerous characteristics, and they must be ranked naturally one beside the other, without differences amongst them except by less important characteristics sufficient to distinguish them.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Thus, well constructed genera are really small }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 families}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , i.e., true parts of the very order of nature.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \