 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 To be sure, often nothing results from these odd matings, above all when they involve very different types, and then the individuals produced are, in general, infertile. But then again, when the disparity is less great, we know that the flaws in question do not occur. Now, this method by itself is sufficient to create varieties gradually which then become races, and which, in time, make up what we call }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 species}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 .}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 In order to evaluate whether the traditional idea of }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 species }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 has some real foundation, let us look again at points which I have already established. They enable us to see the following:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (1) All organic bodies of our earth are true products of nature, which she has brought forth successively over a long period of time;}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (2) In her progress, nature began, and begins again every day, by creating the simplest organic bodies, and she does not directly create anything except by this process, that is to say, by these first beginnings of organic structure which are designated by the expression }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 spontaneous generation}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 .}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (3) The first beginnings of animals and plants were formed in appropriate places and circumstances. Once the faculties of a commencing life and of organic movement were established, these animals and plants of necessity gradually developed organs, and, in time, they diversified these organs, as well as their parts.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (4) The faculty of growth in each portion of an organic body is inherent in the first effects of life; it gave rise to different ways of multiplication and reproduction of individuals. In this process, the progress acquired in the composition of the organic structure and in the shape and diversity of parts was maintained.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (5) With the help of a sufficient lapse of time, of circumstances which were necessarily favourable, of changes which every point on the surface of the earth has successively undergone, in a word, with the assistance of the power which new situations and habits have for modifying the organs of a body endowed with life, all those which exist now have been imperceptibly shaped just as we see them.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 (6) Finally, after a sequence of events like the above, living bodies have each experienced greater or lesser changes in the condition of their organic structure and their parts. What we call }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 species }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 have been created in this way imperceptibly and successively among them; they have a constancy which is only relative to their condition and cannot be as old as nature.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \