 mammal which we call the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 bat}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  also has a carinate sternum.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 All the blood of birds passes once more through their lung before reaching the other parts of the body. Thus, they breathe completely by their lung, like the animals of the first rank. After them, no known animal has a similar system.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af6 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af6 \loch \f6 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \sl276 \slmult1 \widctlpar \keep0 \keepn0 \aspalpha \aspnum \toplinepunct0 \faauto \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \